HEDGEHOG OS — HUMAN CROSS-DOMAIN DRS BRIDGE WALKTHROUGH v0.1

1. WHAT THIS DEMO IS

This is a human-readable walkthrough over the committed Cross-domain DRS Bridge Proof v0.1. The proof observes local proof-only DRS bridge traversal over already established bounded semantic coupling edges.

Root authorizes traversal. Traversal informs Root review, but it does not decide, finalize, execute, or transfer authority.

This is not External DRS, global DRS, a public semantic fabric, production persistence, remote retrieval, connector/API access, Gemini, network, Telegram, Marennya, UP, or live agent execution.

2. WHY THIS COMES AFTER DUAL COUPLING

Dual Fractal Coupling established two bounded parent DACs: certificate_parent_dac and travel_parent_dac.

It also established bounded semantic coupling edges for insurance_certificate and payment_receipt.

DRS Bridge v0.1 does not invent new authority. It locally traverses those already established bounded semantic edges.

A coupling edge is the bounded semantic relation. DRS bridge traversal is the local, reviewed trace over that relation.

3. SOURCE AND TARGET DOMAINS

Source domain: certificate_parent_dac / APP-77 / CERT-310.
Target domain: travel_parent_dac / TRAVEL-900 / ITIN-44.

